1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:03,109
The Weather widget gives a shared
board a quick read on current

2
00:00:03,109 --> 00:00:04,710
conditions and the days ahead.

3
00:00:05,110 --> 00:00:07,369
Here it shows Chicago in Fahrenheit.

4
00:00:07,809 --> 00:00:11,600
A security supervisor can use the
same display for outdoor posts,

5
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:15,100
and a search and rescue coordinator
can use it for a staging area.

6
00:00:15,469 --> 00:00:17,920
In Configure, open Weather Widget.

7
00:00:18,289 --> 00:00:21,869
The Units choices are
Standard, Metric and Imperial.

8
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:27,620
Standard uses Kelvin, Metric uses
Celsius, and Imperial uses Fahrenheit.

9
00:00:27,969 --> 00:00:30,790
Pick the units your team
expects to read at a glance.

10
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:32,870
This board starts in Imperial.

11
00:00:33,110 --> 00:00:34,290
Select Metric.

12
00:00:34,709 --> 00:00:38,360
The latitude and longitude fields
choose the location for this widget.

13
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:43,170
Here we enter forty-one point eight
five north and negative eighty-seven

14
00:00:43,170 --> 00:00:45,019
point six nine for longitude.

15
00:00:45,449 --> 00:00:48,430
Keep the minus sign for a
location west of Greenwich.

16
00:00:48,819 --> 00:00:52,320
Leaving both values at zero lets
the app use the department map

17
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:53,759
center when it is available.

18
00:00:54,010 --> 00:00:56,140
Give the forecast room to breathe.

19
00:00:56,739 --> 00:01:02,199
In this example, we increase Width to
five and Height to four, then select Save.

20
00:01:02,579 --> 00:01:05,890
A larger tile makes it easier
for a team to read the upcoming

21
00:01:05,890 --> 00:01:07,230
days from across a room.

22
00:01:07,510 --> 00:01:10,880
Back on the board, verify the
city as well as the units.

23
00:01:11,239 --> 00:01:14,630
The Chicago widget now shows
temperature in Celsius and wind

24
00:01:14,630 --> 00:01:16,150
speed in meters per second.

25
00:01:16,549 --> 00:01:20,200
The forecast rows give the team a
quick way to compare the coming days.

26
00:01:20,570 --> 00:01:23,829
These are live readings, so
the exact values will change.

27
00:01:23,990 --> 00:01:28,200
Reopen Weather Widget settings and check
that Metric, the coordinates, and the

28
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:30,380
larger tile size survived the save.

29
00:01:30,889 --> 00:01:34,730
A community paramedicine team could
center a board on its outreach area;

30
00:01:35,079 --> 00:01:38,609
a wildland contractor could center
one on its base of operations.

31
00:01:39,149 --> 00:01:43,450
Use the separate Weather Alerts widget to
review alert headlines and instructions.
